  "summary": "A traditional leather tanning and dyeing process producing distinctive colored leathers for artisan goods.",
  "description": "Characterized by vegetable-tanned leather dyed with natural pigments including henna, saffron, and pomegranate, resulting in rich reds, browns, and yellows. This aesthetic developed in the Chouara quarter of Fez, utilizing ancient techniques passed down through generations, creating durable materials for bags, shoes, and furniture.",
